Unified Windows Suite
=====================

A merger of two independently developed MIT-licensed projects. Both copyright
notices are reproduced in LICENSE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Win11Debloat            Copyright (c) 2020 Raphire
                        https://github.com/Raphire/Win11Debloat

Provides the architectural base: the declarative Features.json catalogue, the
registry tweak library (249 .reg files with 65 undo files and 91 sysprep
variants), the appx and provisioned-package removal engine, offline user-hive
targeting, structured registry backup and restore, the XAML interface, the
localisation layer, and the Pester suite.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ultimate Windows Setup Toolkit
                        Copyright (c) 2025-2026
                        Network & Firewall Technicians / OffTrackMedia

Provides the capabilities Win11Debloat has no equivalent for: the application
installer across winget, Chocolatey and Scoop with a 167-app catalogue; the
hardware profiler and performance-tier scoring; the driver manager with DISM
export and pnputil restore; and the performance optimiser covering power plans,
memory management, virtual memory, disk cleanup, startup programs and DNS.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DELIBERATE OMISSION
-------------------
This suite contains no product-activation, licence-bypass or key-generation
functionality.

The Ultimate Windows Setup Toolkit shipped modules/Activator.psm1, which
downloaded and executed a third-party activation script at run time, plus a
duplicate implementation inside its debloat menu. Neither is present here, and
neither is reimplemented under another name.

Use a licence you own. Windows and Office licences are sold by Microsoft and by
authorised resellers, and a retail licence can be moved to new hardware through
the Microsoft account it is tied to.
